    "description": "**PLACEHOLDER — raised 2026-09-01, to be specced before work starts.**\n\n## Requirement\n\nReps must not be able to directly edit fields on the following record pages:\n\n* Operator\n* Partner\n* Deal\n* Brand Ambassador\n* Deal Rep Assignment (DRA)\n* Affiliate Link\n\nThese pages should be read-only for reps. Any value a rep legitimately needs to change should be written by a flow, quick action, or automation running in system context — not by inline edit or the standard Edit button.\n\n## Proposed solution (draft — not yet designed)\n\n* Enforce at **field-level security** on the rep permission set group (Read, not Edit) so the restriction holds on list views, inline edit, API and layouts — page-layout read-only alone is not enough.\n* Keep object-level Edit only where a flow needs it, and have the flow run in system context so the rep's own FLS does not block it.\n* Expose the sanctioned rep actions as buttons or quick actions on each page; remove the standard Edit and inline-edit affordances from rep layouts.\n\n## Open questions\n\n* Which fields (if any) do reps genuinely need write access to today? Each one becomes a flow instead.\n* Does this apply to record creation as well, or edit only?\n* Interaction with the existing rep-facing POCs (Sign-Up screen, Rep Home Page) — those write via flow already; confirm nothing depends on direct rep edit.\n* Size and effort TBD once the field list is confirmed.\n\n",
